The important thing is that the architecture survived contact with code:

StoryIR + PatternBook \rightarrow MusicIR-ish\ events \rightarrow Renderer \rightarrow Audio

while the same visual scene remains fixed. The two buttons really are changing the interpretive field, not the scene itself. That’s exactly the experiment we wanted.

And I like several choices in here. STORY_IR is grammar-independent, GRAMMARS contains the transferable relationship logic, and webAudioSynthRenderer is replaceable. That means the crude browser synth isn’t baked into the concept. Later you can replace:

webAudioSynthRenderer

with:

orchestralRenderer
rockSongRenderer
generativeMusicModel
sampleLibraryRenderer
liveInstrumentRenderer

without rewriting the underlying narrative representation.

