There are also a few small code things I’d clean up before treating this as the base repo version. The starfield currently drifts offscreen without wrapping; the impact burst depends on hitting a very small 28.00–28.05 frame window; switching grammars kills sustained notes that began before the switch, so the new treatment can briefly lack whatever musical state should already be active; and the current “motifs” are effectively fixed note arrays rather than true transformable symbolic motif objects.

None of those invalidate the MVP.

In fact, this is exactly the kind of prototype we wanted: cheap enough that its shortcomings reveal what the next abstraction needs to be.

